// Permit Read only when TWO independent regex guardrails agree the document
// is safe: it must match an allowed-charset pattern (lowercase letters and
// digits only) AND contain no digits at all. Each check lives in its own
// `when guardrails { … }` clause; like multiple Cedar `when` clauses, they
// are conjoined — the rule fires iff both hold. The two checks are genuinely
// independent: the charset check rejects uppercase / punctuation, while the
// digit check rejects digits that the charset check alone would allow.
//
// This is the runnable, regex-backed analog of the reference
// `documentation_0406_multiple_guardrail_clauses`, which carries two
// `when guardrails` clauses over two different classifiers.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when guardrails {
    Strings::Matches(context.input.document, "^[a-z0-9]+$").matched == true
}
when guardrails {
    Strings::DigitCount(context.input.document).count == 0
};
